Luciernaga function notes

:::HolisticQCParse - WORKS FOR BD WITH CAVEATS
Reads BD fcs files and applies gating template before parsing data into CSV form. Gating templates are first passed 
to :::GateCheck, which doesn't function correctly when run manually, but doesn't seem to have any effect when run 
within :::HolisticQCParse. Might work with Aurora data?

:::QC_Plots - WORKS
Takes laser-specific gain/MFI/rCV data generated within instrument qmd files, converts to proper formatting and 
passes to :::LevyJennings to generate plots, then collates the generated plots. Has functionality for adding info 
regarding FSE visits, but I have not examined that yet.

:::LevyJennings - WORKS
Takes data generated by :::QC_Plots and creates corresponding ggplot graphs accordingly. If parameter names are in Aurora 
format (eg. R3, UV12, B1, etc), colors graph lines to match laser. If not, graph lines are black. Can create individual
and comparison plots, only individual plots have been assessed. 

:::CurentData - WORKS
lubridates data from instrument, arranges by date and time. Has slightly different function based on if it's Aurora 
or BD data

:::VisualQCSummary - WORKS
Presents data from archived CSVs in tidy format, passes to :::QCSummaryCheck to determine individual dectector pass/fail,
  then assigns green/red accordingly
  
:::QCSummaryCheck - WORKS FOR AURORA
Checks for gain and rCV flags from Aurora QC csvs. Does not seem to do anything with BD instruments.

:::SmallTable - WORKS
Takes output of :::VisualQCSummary and presents in table form with cells colored green/red based on pass/fail status.
Output is what's shown on website home/index page